.TH "NIAC" "1" "Sep 2026" "NIAC" "NIAC Manual"

.SH NAME
niac-version - Print the version, commit and build metadata


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac version [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the build metadata compiled into this binary.

.PP
The fields are the ones the daemon serves at /__version — version, commit,
buildTime, uiBuildHash and releaseTrain — so a deployment check can compare
the binary on disk against the daemon it started.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for version

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Print version metadata as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Human-readable
  niac version

  # For scripts
  niac version --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac(1)\fP


